meta {
  name: 15-service-type-validation
  seq: 16
}

docs {
  # Service Type Header Validation Tests

  ## Concept Overview

  SIF 3.3 §5.1 defines that the `serviceType` HTTP header must match the URL path pattern.
  Different paths accept different serviceType values:

  | URL path pattern | Valid serviceType values |
  |---|---|
  | `/requests/*` | OBJECT, SERVICEPATH, XQUERYTEMPLATE |
  | `/services/*` | FUNCTIONAL |
  | `/events` | OBJECT, UTILITY, FUNCTIONAL, SERVICEPATH, XQUERYTEMPLATE, SERVICE |
  | Utility paths | UTILITY |

  The gateway's `ServiceTypeValidationFilter` rejects requests with mismatched
  serviceType values with HTTP 400 before they reach authorization or connectors.

  ## Test Purpose

  Verify that the broker correctly rejects requests with invalid serviceType values:
  - GET `/requests/{object}` with `serviceType: FUNCTIONAL` → 400
  - GET `/requests/{object}` with `serviceType: UTILITY` → 400
  - GET `/requests/{object}` with `serviceType: INVALID_VALUE` → 400
  - POST `/services/{name}` with `serviceType: OBJECT` → 400
  - POST `/services/{name}` with `serviceType: XQUERYTEMPLATE` → 400

  ## Prerequisites

  - This section is self-contained (creates its own domain/solution)
  - An external provider endpoint must be running at the URL configured in
    `immediateProviderEndpointUrl`
  - The provider must serve "StudentPersonals"

  ## Expected Behavior

  - Setup creates a zone, provider env, consumer env, ACLs, and provider registration
  - Consumer has QUERY access so requests would normally succeed
  - Negative tests prove that invalid serviceType causes HTTP 400 rejection
  - The 400 response contains the invalid value, path, and valid values list
  - Teardown removes all section-specific resources

  ## SIF Specification Reference

  - SIF 3.3 §5.1 — serviceType header validation
  - SIF 3.7 §5.1 — serviceType / URL path mapping
}
